posts.body:
Enemy skills are decided at the begining of the turn (early enough so all the actions - actors' and enemies' - can be ordered by speed), but the targets of the actions are picked at the last moment.
For example if a character has a high speed provoke skill that dramatically increases (or reduces) their TGR, enemies will be able to pick their target using the updated TGR value and not the TGR value they had in the begining of the turn.
And enemies' attacks won't be canceled due to invalid targets (dead characters).
This is MZ default code, but I guess it was similar in older makers :
Code:
BattleManager.startAction = function() {
    const subject = this._subject;
    const action = subject.currentAction();
    const targets = action.makeTargets();
    this._phase = "action";
    this._action = action;
    this._targets = targets;
    subject.cancelMotionRefresh();
    subject.useItem(action.item());
    this._action.applyGlobal();
    this._logWindow.startAction(subject, action, targets);
};
makeTargets() is called during the startAction() method execution.
A "read their mind" plugin would need huge rework of the battle flow and also to solve many problems such as the TGR changing, invalid targets.
